DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
       The  ppuutteennvv()  function  adds or changes the value of environment vari‐
       ables.  The argument _s_t_r_i_n_g is of the form _n_a_m_e=_v_a_l_u_e.   If  _n_a_m_e  does
       not already exist in the environment, then _s_t_r_i_n_g is added to the envi‐
       ronment.  If _n_a_m_e does exist, then the value of _n_a_m_e in the environment
       is  changed  to _v_a_l_u_e.  The string pointed to by _s_t_r_i_n_g becomes part of
       the environment, so altering the string changes the environment.

RREETTUURRNN VVAALLUUEE
       The ppuutteennvv() function returns zero on success.  On failure, it  returns
       a nonzero value, and _e_r_r_n_o is set to indicate the error.

